{% section tone="grey" %}
## African drumming classes FAQs

{% faq %}
{% question title="Do I need any drumming experience?" %}
Not at all. Our African drumming classes welcome complete beginners, so we break every rhythm down step by step. In fact, you don’t need coordination to start, because we’ll have you grooving in no time!
{% /question %}

{% question title="Can children join the drumming class?" %}
Yes. The class is mainly for adults, but children aged 8 and up are welcome to join in too.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Do I need my own drum?" %}
No. You’re welcome to bring your own drum, but you can also hire one at class.
{% /question %}

{% question title="How often do you learn a new rhythm?" %}
Every 4 weeks. During that time, you learn 2 to 3 parts of the rhythm on the djembe. Then we play them together as a group.
{% /question %}

{% question title="What is a djembe?" %}
The djembe is a goblet-shaped hand drum from West Africa. You play it with your bare hands, and it’s the main drum you’ll learn in class.
{% /question %}
{% /faq %}
{% /section %}

